Description: avfilter/tonemapx: build only the input format list that the filter keeps
 With an output format named, query_formats() built the list of all
 the filter's input formats and attached it to the input link. A few
 lines on it built the list of the input formats whose plane layout
 matches the output format and attached that one to the same link.
 ff_formats_ref() stores a list in the link without releasing the list
 the link held, so the first list stayed allocated and unreachable: 48
 bytes each time a graph with the filter is configured. With the
 default, format=same, the filter attaches one list and did not leak.
 .
 Build only the second list. The formats the filter accepts and offers
 do not change.
Author: Streamarr
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-11
---
Index: FFmpeg/libavfilter/vf_tonemapx.c
===================================================================
--- FFmpeg.orig/libavfilter/vf_tonemapx.c
+++ FFmpeg/libavfilter/vf_tonemapx.c
@@ -1711,10 +1711,6 @@ static int query_formats(AVFilterContext *ctx)
         s->format = AV_PIX_FMT_NONE;
     } else {
         int i, j = 0;
-        formats = ff_make_format_list(in_pix_fmts);
-        res = ff_formats_ref(formats, &ctx->inputs[0]->outcfg.formats);
-        if (res < 0)
-            return res;
         if (s->format == AV_PIX_FMT_NONE) {
             av_log(ctx, AV_LOG_ERROR, "Unrecognized pixel format: %s\n", s->format_str);
             return AVERROR(EINVAL);
